# .trivyignore — Trivy CVE exceptions
# Format: one CVE/GHSA ID per line (optionally with expiry: id exp:YYYY-MM-DD)
#
# HOW TO USE (local scan):
#   trivy image --severity HIGH,CRITICAL --ignore-unfixed \
#               --ignorefile .trivyignore <image>
#
# POLICY: Only entries here are for CVEs where the vulnerable code is:
#   (a) vendored INSIDE a tool (pip or setuptools), AND
#   (b) NOT callable from application code at runtime, AND
#   (c) the safe version of the tool is already installed (verified in build logs)
#
# Review each entry when upgrading pip / setuptools to remove stale ignores.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── pip/_vendor/msgpack ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Trivy source: /usr/local/lib/python3.12/site-packages/pip-*.dist-info/METADATA
#   pip vendors msgpack internally (pip/_vendor/msgpack/).
#   The application-installed msgpack (>=1.2.1) is clean.
#   pip's vendored copy cannot be upgraded without rebuilding pip itself.
#   The vulnerable code path (Unpacker reuse) is only exercised by pip
#   during package download caching — never by FastAPI app code at runtime.
# CVE: https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964

# ── pip/_vendor/setuptools (ensurepip residue) ───────────────────────────────
# Trivy source: pip's METADATA references an older setuptools as a bundled dep.
#   Installed setuptools in site-packages is >=78.1.1 (verified in build logs).
#   The vulnerable setuptools PackageIndex code is only invoked when pip
#   calls setuptools to install packages — not reachable from app runtime.
# CVE: https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-47273
CVE-2025-47273

# ── setuptools/_vendor/jaraco.context ────────────────────────────────────────
# Trivy source: setuptools/_vendor/jaraco/ internal vendor directory.
#   Installed jaraco.context in site-packages is >=6.1.0 (verified in build logs).
#   Only used internally by setuptools during package operations, not at runtime.
# CVE: https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-23949
CVE-2026-23949

# ── pip/_vendor/wheel ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Trivy source: pip or setuptools bundles an older wheel as a build backend.
#   Installed wheel in site-packages is >=0.46.2 (verified in build logs).
#   wheel is a build tool; it is not imported or used at application runtime.
# CVE: https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-24049
CVE-2026-24049
